From 2d0cf1a24681167eacb0832fd69f5ef7e6c5c225 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: deck <jenergy@tiscali.it>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 19:14:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Sprint: first-controller keypad swap + FPS fix (under
 JZINTV_SPRINT)

Two more Sprint-only features, both gated directly by JZINTV_SPRINT (no
extra feature macro; only the in-game menu keeps its own ADD_JZINTV_MENU).

First-controller keypad swap (cfg/mapping.c): the Sprint's first (left)
hand controller has its keypad top/bottom rows wired swapped, so 1/2/3
act as 7/8/9 and vice versa (4/5/6 unchanged). Swap the WHOLE binding --
storage slot AND emitted hardware code -- between KP1<->KP7, KP2<->KP8,
KP3<->KP9 for PD0L. Swapping the slot as well as the code keeps the
emulated machine and the in-game menu in agreement (the menu resolves a
keypad digit from the bound slot, so a code-only swap fixes games but
leaves the menu inverted). Done at the mapping level, so it covers any
input source (keyboard and USB pad via hackfile). First controller only.

FPS fix (gfx/gfx_sdl2.c): pin the software scaler to native 160x200, use
a fixed 1280x720 window, and let the SDL2 hardware renderer do the
upscale in gfx_flip -- moving the stretch off the ARM CPU to hold 60 FPS.
The render dest {160,0,960,720} is a 4:3 pillarbox, so a Sprint build is
forced 4:3 for free; --aspect-4-3 now only applies to the non-Sprint
builds, which are unchanged (gfx_flip alternates: JZINTV_SPRINT -> FPS
fix, else -> the --aspect-4-3 path). Wide mode via border_x==40; -v crops
overscan.

Update ReleaseNotes_20260816.txt. build.sh is intentionally untouched.
